comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:07:04.041Z",codex,Created after reconciling pmc-wvnz so the completed 100/100/100 contract remains distinct from this new four-dimensional reporting requirement.
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:07:04.041Z",codex,Do not implement this by duplicating the line percentage under a statements label. Inspect the primary Node/V8 and any candidate instrumentation APIs before selecting a provider.
  "2026-08-20T21:19:04.644Z",codex,"Measured evidence on 2026-08-20: npm run release:check passed 387 tests before the PR #148 review follow-up,and the Node/V8 table reported all nine measured sources plus aggregate at exactly 100.00 percent lines,branches,and functions. The same output contains no statements column,which is the gap this item owns."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T21:07:04.041Z",codex,Exact coverage claims must name the dimensions the authoritative tool actually measures; semantic equivalence needs evidence when a required metric is absent.
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/coverage-gate.ts,project,Fail-closed Node/V8 coverage runner and source inventory
  package.json,project,Coverage thresholds and release scripts
tests[2]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,pm_context_mode,note}:
  npm run coverage,project,600,tracker,Must report exact four-dimensional coverage
  "npm run release:check",project,900,tracker,Authoritative package gate
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://nodejs.org/api/test.html#collecting-code-coverage",project,Primary Node test-runner coverage contract to verify during implementation
body: "## Scope\n\nPreserve the existing Node/V8 all-source inventory and exact three-dimensional gate while establishing a genuine, reviewable statement metric. Prefer primary runtime/tooling contracts and measured counter data over naming assumptions.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThis item does not authorize lowering thresholds, excluding executable source, or treating the line percentage as a fourth result without a testable proof."
